  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-ENC48/procedure/01/cause">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#PossibleCause"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Dell ENC48 possible cause 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:causeText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A storage topology issue is detected on the controller identified in the message. Some of the possible reasons are: 1) Incorrect cable connections such as loose, damaged, or improperly routed SAS cables. 2) Firmware incompatibility such as different SAS devices (like RAID controllers and expanders) might require the same firmware version to work correctly within a topology. 3) Exceeding enclosure limits such as a SAS controller may only support a certain number of enclosures, and connecting more than supported can cause an error. 4) Unsupported devices in the configuration.</diag:causeText>
  </rdf:Description>
